WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.530
When it comes to X-Men: Dark Phoenix, it seems
that things aren't looking too bright.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:10.340
The sequel to 2016's X-Men Apocalypse, Dark
Phoenix is finally nearing its June 7 launch

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.769
after stumbling through multiple delays and
an in-depth round of reshoots.

00:00:14.769 --> 00:00:18.960
Sadly, whatever it was they filmed during
those reshoots may not have done much to improve

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.369
the movie's fortunes.

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:25.249
In fact, the most recent Dark Phoenix-related
news could spell even more trouble, serving

00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:27.579
as what could be a fatal blow for the flick.

00:00:27.579 --> 00:00:32.921
According to journalist Skyler Shuler, studio
20th Century Fox recently held a test screening

00:00:32.921 --> 00:00:37.750
for Dark Phoenix to collect audience's reactions
to the latest cut and gauge how well the film

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.920
might do upon its wide theatrical release
this summer.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.090
What Fox likely hoped would be a successful
pre-premiere showing apparently turned out

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.470
disastrous, as the screening is said to have
completely bombed.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.120
This is now the third Dark Phoenix test showing
that has garnered an unsavory response from

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.120
viewers.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.090
Shuler alleged on Twitter: "Another X-Men:
Dark Phoenix test screening, and guess what?

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:02.440
I now have talked to 6 people who all went
to 3 different test screenings, and all of

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.900
them have told me the screenings were BAD."

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.250
"Don't you say that!!"

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.250
One fan responded:

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.790
"I went to one of the screenings.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:13.610
Everybody LAUGHED SO HARD in a scene supposed
to be so serious."

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:15.580
"NO!

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.560
No…"

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.640
And Shuler replied: "I think I know what scene
you're referring to."

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:27.400
And this isn't even the first time the movie
has failed to wow test audiences.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.400
Earlier this month, Shuler relayed that Dark
Phoenix was shaping up to earn a spot in the

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.910
lower echelon of Fox's superhero films.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:39.570
That would put it right alongside the slapped-together,
incoherent, 2015 Fantastic Four reboot, which

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:44.450
is better known online as "Fant4stic" because
of the film's, uh, questionable marketing

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.450
campaign.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.000
Tweeted Shuler on January 2:

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.870
"Based on what I have heard, this movie [could]
be Fant4stic level BAD."

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.530
"She's gone…

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.780
She's gone…

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.840
She's…"

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.229
Of course, this movie's been in trouble for
a long, long while, if reports are to be believed.

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:09.060
The very first crummy Dark Phoenix test screening
apparently took place sometime before March

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.060
2018.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.840
That's when Collider published an exclusive
report claiming that writer-director Simon

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.790
Kinberg and Fox executives had screened Dark
Phoenix for a test audience, quote, "to see

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:22.980
what was working and what wasn't," and that
the response to the movie pushed the Dark

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.730
Phoenix team to delay the movie's release
and order additional photography.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:31.000
While a movie going on with reshoots doesn't
always indicate poor test screening response,

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.400
it seems to be the case with Dark Phoenix.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.790
ScreenRant reported at the time, quote, "Dark
Phoenix's delay has been heavily influenced

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.170
by reshoots in response to test screenings."

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.900
Metro UK followed up in September 2018 that
the reshoots were a direct response to, quote,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.150
"devastating test screening reactions."

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.200
Fox's plans for reshoots were made even more
difficult because of the logistical headaches

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.569
involved in re-assembling a cast full of Hollywood
A-Listers, actors like Sophie Turner as Jean

00:02:57.569 --> 00:03:02.480
Grey, Michael Fassbender as Magneto, James
McAvoy as Charles Xavier, Jennifer Lawrence

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.450
as Mystique, and Nicholas Hoult as Beast,
among several others.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.910
As a result, the reshoots were scheduled for
fall of 2018, pushing Dark Phoenix from its

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:16.129
intended November 2018 launch to a February
14, 2019 one.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:20.950
Reshoots reportedly began on August 31, 2018,
but may not have wrapped before Fox rolled

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.709
out the first trailer for Dark Phoenix at
the end of September.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:28.569
That footage revealed that Dark Phoenix had
been delayed a second time, moving from Valentine's

00:03:28.569 --> 00:03:33.459
Day 2019 to June 7, its current and unlikely-to-change
debut date.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:37.420
From there, it looks as though Fox conducted
the second test screening for Dark Phoenix

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:42.459
after releasing the first trailer, holding
it at the tail end of 2018 or the start of

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:43.459
2019.

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:46.480
But judging by the Tweets and fan-reports
that have come out since then, it doesn't

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.280
sound as if the reshoots have done much to
help the film's reception among test audiences.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.510
"No… noooo."

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:57.629
If Dark Phoenix turns out to be as rough as
test screening attendees say it is, it would

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:01.680
be a sad way for the X-Men franchise to go
out before the characters shuffle over to

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:05.239
the Marvel Studios wing of the Walt Disney
Company.

